Z||000038||batboy||01-22-2000||06:01 PM||||I'm hoping someone will scan that magazine pic of Phil's hot little ride and post it. Monkey, I know what you mean. As much as I brag about the ol' Batmobile, most of my work has been replacing worn out parts and beefing up brakes and suspension. Hotrod Magazine would take one look at my beast with it's crappy original paint job, banged up dash corners, hole in the seat, etc... and they would either laugh or just shake their heads in wonder and walk away. However, it's a LOW budget project (about $3000 total), it's FUN to drive, it's FAST, and it's MINE! Remember, a V8 kit cost about just $2000 by itself.||||reg||1
Z||000039||batboy||01-22-2000||06:10 PM||||Oops, better make that about $3500 total investment in the Batmobile. I forgot to add in the stereo equipment. Add another $500 for the new tires I need, another $2500 or $3000 for the engine I'm building for it, $2000 to $2500 for a paint job, body mods, and to have the interior redone. Hmmmm... suddenly, it's no longer a low budget project! But, it will still be a fraction of what a new car costs and a whale of a lot better than a new car.||||reg||1
Z||000040||Monkeyman||01-22-2000||06:14 PM||||I'll bet HR mag would still enjoy a pic and description of the Batmobile.  How many Fieros have V8s?  Once you get the time/money to finish it I'd rush to send some info/pics in to them.  They'd be crazy NOT to do something about it then.||||reg||1
